From 642502e1cf497e142e02a8873bf8fd4f10e655c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gavin John <gavinnjohn@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 20:46:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 22/40] demux: adaptive: give a stream another chance when
 seeking

A stream whose demuxer fails to start is marked invalid to stop
doBufferize() from trying again on every pass, which would spin. Nothing
ever marks it valid again, so the flag outlives the condition that set
it: PlaylistManager::setPosition() skips invalid streams and gives up
when none are left, and HLS usually has a single stream per variant, so
one transient failure to build a demuxer leaves the whole session
unseekable while the demux object stays open. updateControlsPosition()
skips them too, so the reported length and position stop moving as well.

A seek is a new attempt rather than a continuation of the loop the guard
was protecting, so clear it there, alongside the end of stream flag and
the rest of the per-position state that resetForNewPosition() already
resets. If starting still fails, both this path and doBufferize() mark
the stream invalid again at once, so a genuinely dead stream costs one
attempt per seek rather than spinning.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 modules/demux/adaptive/Streams.cpp | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/modules/demux/adaptive/Streams.cpp b/modules/demux/adaptive/Streams.cpp
index d476d77f2b..645063e336 100644
--- a/modules/demux/adaptive/Streams.cpp
+++ b/modules/demux/adaptive/Streams.cpp
@@ -152,6 +152,8 @@ bool AbstractStream::resetForNewPosition(vlc_tick_t seekMediaTime)
     inrestart = false;
     needrestart = false;
     discontinuity = false;
+    /* A seek is a fresh attempt; the failure paths raise this again. */
+    valid = true;
     if(!demuxer || demuxer->needsRestartOnSeek()) /* needs (re)start */
     {
         delete currentChunk;
